WEBVTT

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:19.150
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:25.180
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.690
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:33.030
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.300
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.800
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.640
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.680
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.310
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.120
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.120
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to the voices before it collapses

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.990
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:10.870
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:22.340
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.110
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.990
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:39.450
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:03.280
Narasaki... Good thing you never had to see it.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.250
Counselor...

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.460
Not anymore. An official notice was given, as well.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.250
I'm used to addressing you that way.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.390
About the burial?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.230
As an exception... a word from
the temporary chief worked.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.180
The owner is Kametsuna Shinsuke.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.940
Probably one of Kujo Mareya's sponsors.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.870
An internal bureaucrat...

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.870
Further pursuit is pointless.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.450
I wonder if she lived here alone,
seeing illusions of her family?

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.460
She had her friends.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.460
You're right.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.710
How did Morimoto look?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.840
Beautiful...

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.840
She got to fall asleep next to the person she loved.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.010
I see.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.390
Have you been sweating? You should change.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.050
Sorry I couldn't make it.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.030
You didn't have a choice.
The doctor told you to rest.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.160
That's not what I mean.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.170
They were a good match.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:36.770
Those two...

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.250
Why did all this have to happen?

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.980
We were all...

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.280
It's all because of that day, ten years ago.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.820
But... without that day,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:55.590
we wouldn't have...

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.100
We wouldn't have all met.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.700
Yeah.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.530
How's Shin doing?

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:19.610
It wasn't the people who left.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.190
Maybe... the boy made them invisible to himself

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.650
by closing his heart from everyone.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:35.070
I don't know why he would do such a
thing, or what need there was to do so.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.660
Morimoto...

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.740
I...

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.080
Did you show that to me?

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.320
About that day...

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.720
My brother's...

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.120
Our...

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.620
Those thoughts are calling
for each other, deep down.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.690
Where is my brother?

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.660
I wanna see him. Jun is with him too, right!?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.920
They...

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.260
won't see you anymore.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:45.040
Because they're aware of the retribution
spreading, filling up all things.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.570
You're needed by that which was
created as something similar to me.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:56.570
To cut me off from the Whale.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.490
Don't go near...

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.050
the other me.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.060
Kanzato-kun?

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.220
I see.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.170
What Kanzato really feared

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.530
was you regaining your memory from that day.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.960
When I saw your clay figure,

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.270
I thought the spear piercing
through the two Personas

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:00.000
looked similar to the sword your Persona wields.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.450
But...

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.480
you said you didn't know what it was.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.220
It made me think it might be related to...

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:14.220
something supporting Kanzato
Ryo's incomparable sense of duty.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.500
The subspecies of Persona that
ruined his beloved family's destiny.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:26.260
To terminate the existence which goes against
providence, he got employed at the organization.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.010
Before he accomplished his goal,

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:33.170
he feared the involvement of his two brothers,

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.680
the awakening of their Personas,

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:38.150
and most of all...

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:44.380
you regaining the memory of murdering
your parents with your Persona.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.530
Half a year ago, when the Marebito
officially started taking action,

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:58.270
you and your brother's return
came at the worst time for him.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.770
Until now, I had no idea.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.040
Of course, if I had remembered
about that time, I would've...

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.850
But why?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.110
Why did he take all the burden himself?

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.420
Because that is his persona.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.770
Even if he didn't take the control
pills to strengthen his mentality...

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:31.030
He always wore his mask as the cold
eldest brother, not once removing it.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.140
I always felt that about him,

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:46.540
so I expected the possibility of him manipulating
Jun-kun to tame the Marebitos' Personas.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:51.390
So you knew my brother was gonna bring
Jun's psyche there from the beginning?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.620
There was no guarantee.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:09:01.460
Our initial plan was to negotiate, using
Jun-kun's power to make them surrender.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:03.660
Plus...

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:09.340
Him taking Jun-kun away once he reunited
with his twin wasn't a part of our plan.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:17.480
The bionoid modeled after Komatsubara Ayane you
encountered was the ultimate existence to Kujo.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:23.260
With it, he could interfere with
the world of unconsciousness.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:30.390
However, this Whale Ayane talks about will
either deny them, or absorb and purify them.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:37.230
You're aware of the special
power your Persona possesses?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:39.060
Yes.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.880
As Kujo Mareya says, if your Persona
is the one last missing puzzle piece,

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:49.610
his goal is to dive into the sea of unconsciousness

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.780
and regain the soul of Ayane,
who became a part of the Whale.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:58.230
He seeks to revive his dearest daughter,
who was lost due to his own mistake.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:02.960
Even after his death, Kujo is trying
to accomplish such a selfish delusion.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.670
We must not have your Persona get absorbed,

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:10.000
nor have them encounter the Whale.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.840
If they make contact, an even
larger distortion will be created,

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.080
and something far worse than the
incident ten years ago may happen.

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.710
How can we end this?

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.280
The last action has been taken.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.050
There's no need for you to fight anymore.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.630
I think...

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.760
I think I know why you can't use your
Persona when you become an adult.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.130
It's not that you lose your Persona...

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:45.970
It's because you're no longer innocent.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:50.570
Because... you're not allowed to be.

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.180
That's an interesting outlook.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:00.410
Shin.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:05.080
About the reason why Kanzato
took Jun-kun with him...

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:25.780
The transfer to Saint Marshall is a day early.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.210
Is there a problem?

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.620
No.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:35.060
However, if this bionoid has absorbed
all of the Marebitos' Complex Personas

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:39.360
and was stabilized by Kanzato Jun's Persona...

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.760
The way we're managing it now will...

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.790
We've kept it in a coma with medication.

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.370
It's rather creepy.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:52.170
But most of it is composed of real human cells

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.200
created from the DNA of Kujo himself.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.070
That aside...

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:06.780
We've found various minor discrepancies
in the reports you've made so far.

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.590
Mostly to Kanzato and Sanada's advantage.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:21.800
Sanada would've taken control of the raid on
Kujo's facility if it weren't caught by our satellites.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.670
I'd like to hear your story.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.080
Who the-!?

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.130
Does your back hurt?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:34.440
Nah.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.640
Try not to wake her up.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.850
She just fell asleep.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.480
We wouldn't have met if the stuff
from ten years ago didn't happen.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.040
I keep telling myself that.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.390
But your situation is way too cruel.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.920
My Persona...

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.320
It wasn't rowdy or anything.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.860
It was just scared.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:07.870
It's nothing but myself I've been trying to suppress.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:12.370
My dad disappeared, and my mom, too...

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:16.980
I got betrayed by relatives and kids at school.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.410
I grew scared of people.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.050
I couldn't think of anything but rebel.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:26.630
It's an idiot's mindset.

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:29.990
Besides, it was easier that way.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:36.330
But I was just running away.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.870
They say Personas are representations of oneself.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:44.740
I was afraid to use it once I realized it was scared.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.920
But when we started hanging out a lot,

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.690
and after I saw my dad again,

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:55.210
I could use it before I knew it.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:02.420
Same goes for Megumi, too. The reason
she's so caring is due to her nature.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:07.870
She keeps saying it's to atone
for letting her brother die.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:15.340
Her other self she despised and
suppressed inside her when she was little.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.280
But now...

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:24.250
To protect something important
to her, it helps her out.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:29.810
It was Megumi's Persona that found
Morimoto in the mountains, after all.

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:32.060
I can't express it right...

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.190
but I know there's a meaning behind it all.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.430
Sorry, Takuro.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.140
No matter what happened in the past,

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:56.210
to us, you're you.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:39.190
About the reason why Kanzato
took Jun-kun with him...

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.690
No, can't be.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:47.060
Let's end Kujo's delusions first, and
then think about a way to see them.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:54.830
The waves... I can't hear them.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.400
Shin-niichan.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.100
Oniichan.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.690
You come help, too.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:43.120
Ryo, you have something to tell us today, right?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:47.490
What is it?

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:48.430
Did you get her pregnant?

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:49.660
Watch it.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:50.530
Yuki.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.190
Well... um...

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.910
Eiko and I are thinking about getting married.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.780
I feel like it's still too soon, but...

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:05.780
Too soon? We're tired of waiting.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:08.180
We were much younger, too.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.820
Congratulations, you two.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:14.020
Congrats, Eiko-oneechan and oniichan.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.420
Thanks.

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:16.350
Congrats.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:18.120
Thank you.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.460
Congrats, Eiko-neecha-

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:28.230
I mean, Eiko-san.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.670
We can call her Eiko-oneechan, right?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:34.770
Yeah, she's gonna be our real sister now.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.440
Oh, yeah.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:40.610
That's right. Everything will
stay the same as before.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:46.110
You need to start thinking
about your future seriously, too.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.480
Y-yeah...

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:52.080
If there's anything I can do, I'll be glad to help.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.550
Thanks...

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:57.020
Why did you choose your job now?

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.760
There was a teacher I looked up to.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.960
You had her too, right? Ms. Tanaka Yoko.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.670
O-oh, yeah.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.010
That's the broad idea.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.000
I see.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:16.620
Ryo-niichan, how did you propose to Eiko-neechan?

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.950
I can't say that out loud here.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.750
Besides...

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.590
Have you not officially proposed to her yet?

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:27.390
Well... not officially.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.860
That's not good!

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.660
You should do it here, then.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.270
Good idea. We'll be the witnesses.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.100
Jun, Yuki, how does that make any sense?

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.070
I agree with them.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.040
Go ahead.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:39.490
Eiko.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.500
Hello?

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:20.950
I got a call from the personnel who
dispatched Nakamura to Saint Marshall

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.980
and was told they can't get a hold of him.

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:26.380
They fired you.

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:28.780
It's none of our concern now.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:30.890
Inui is also out of reach.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.730
What!? Could they have caught him?

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:36.460
Regardless, I'm heading to the facility.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.620
Worst case scenario, we will proceed with that plan.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.800
Mommy, where are you?

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:05.320
Kanzato!

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.960
Sanada... Stop getting in the way.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:57.680
Itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:57.710
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:03.750
Wasureta huri wo shitetan darou
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:09.990
Chiisana mado akeru yuuki mo naku
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:15.330
kiseki wo matteta
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:25.370
ushinau mono nado nakatta anohi no yona
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:30.710
mujakisa wa mou naikedo
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:36.880
namida wo nugutta ato niwa
After wiping away the tears

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:42.820
atarashii jibun ni deaeru
I'll be able to meet a new self

00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:42.860
Even if I lose everything

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:46.790
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
Even if I lose everything

00:22:46.790 --> 00:22:52.970
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
There are still some things to discover

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:58.840
kesenai kizumo itsuka
Even the scars that remain

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:06.010
watashi rashii hokori ni dekiru
will someday become my pride

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:13.550
The wedge became a sword.

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:16.790
Entrusted with the sword was a child of release.

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:19.860
The sea was calm with hollow emptiness.

00:23:19.860 --> 00:23:23.330
A whale sways in confusion in a blue distortion.

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:26.830
Filled with agonizing feathers.

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:31.870
Atonement, relief, and rest.

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:35.380
Together with his sleep.

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:38.610
With the inner glow.
